--If a king finds his enemy troubled by his neighbour or in other ways, if he feels strong in his hereditary army, if his neighbour is an ally, he can under- take the march in the month of Citra, मार्गशीर्ष and when the planets are in his favour; he must engage after consult- ing the place and time; if rainy season there must be much of infantry and elephants; if spring or winter, chariots and horse; if summer camels or mules, and in other seasons, the fourfold army; the way must be such that yavasa (food) and fuel are available all along; after consultation with ministers and at an auspicious hour he must start; much importance is attached to the शकुनम् (good omens) and [page३-027+ ३९] dreams;
